Tom, Jukka and Darshan's "dump character" patch will make the game write 
your character's inventory, kill list, conduct information and 
intrinsics (everything it lists on the screen and some more) to a file 
when the game ends.  But I like to play on the public servers, where I 
couldn't access the file even if they used that patch.  So, here's a 
idea for a patch just for people running public servers.

Instead of fopen'ing '/tmp/%n', how about obtaining an email address and 
popen'ing 'mailx -s "Obituary for %n" %a' instead?  '%a' would be an 
email address set in your OPTIONS file. (Or maybe an environment 
variable?  See below.)

The only difficulty I see is someone giving a bad email address.  Worst 
case, someone else gets an unexpected/unwanted email when a character 
dies, but I don't see that as being too spammy.  I suppose the server 
could use some technique to request and validate an address outside of 
the game, and then set up an environment variable once it checks out, 
but that seems a bit of a hassle.

And, oh yeah, the mail daemon needs to get mentioned somehow as well. 
Maybe something like, "The mail daemon appears and writes your 
obituary." at the beginning of the dump and "The mail daemon sends your 
obituary to %a" at the end.


